Description: agentic coding tool for the terminal
 Claude Code runs in a terminal, reads and edits a project in place, runs
 the commands a change needs and drives git, taking its instructions in
 prose. It signs in to an Anthropic account and does its work by calling
 the Claude models over the network.
 .
 Anthropic publishes no Debian package and licenses the program under terms
 that grant no right to redistribute it, so this package ships none of it.
 It records the release to install and the SHA-256 of every build of that
 release; its postinst downloads the build matching the machine's
 architecture from Anthropic's own download service, checks it against the
 recorded digest and installs it as /usr/lib/claude-code/claude. Installing
 therefore needs network access.
 .
 Claude Code recognises an installation that dpkg owns and turns its own
 updater off, leaving the version to apt.
